|marrow bone]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] apple [[Cookbook:Brandy|brandy]]\n* 2 cups dry white [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* 4 cups beef [[Cookbook:Broth|broth]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] cloves, pressed or [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallots]], minced\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]] leaves\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 300°F.\n#Mix all of the ingredients together.\n#Place in a deep [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|casserole]] or [[Cookbook:Dutch Oven|Dutch oven]] with a tight fitting lid. Then, wrap the casserole completely in [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]].\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 10–12 hours. Remove bones before serving.\n\n[[Category:French recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for casserole]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wine]]\n[[Category:Braised recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brandy]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tripes à la mode de Caen (Norman Stewed Tripe)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 lb tripe, cut into 2-inch squares","sourceText":"6 lb tripe, cut into 2-inch squares","amountText":"6 lb tripe, cut into 2-inch squares","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 calf's foot, boned and cut into pieces","sourceText":"1 calf's foot, boned and cut into pieces","amountText":"1 calf's foot, boned and cut into pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 lb marrow bone","sourceText":"2 lb marrow bone","amountText":"2 lb marrow bone","amount":null,"unit":null